189
00:05:58,999 --> 00:06:01,501
Two: ask for the orders with no token,

190
00:06:01,501 --> 00:06:04,530
and write the status code in answers dot text,

191
00:06:04,530 --> 00:06:05,913
like this: no log in,

192
00:06:05,913 --> 00:06:06,308
colon,

193
00:06:06,308 --> 00:06:07,362
then the number.

194
00:06:07,912 --> 00:06:08,811
Three: as Bob,

195
00:06:08,811 --> 00:06:10,481
try to delete product one.

196
00:06:10,481 --> 00:06:13,500
Write the status code after the word forbidden,

197
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:13,885
colon.

198
00:06:14,435 --> 00:06:17,850
Four: find Alice's password in secrets dot E N V,

199
00:06:17,850 --> 00:06:18,965
log in as Alice,

200
00:06:18,965 --> 00:06:20,707
and delete product three.

201
00:06:21,257 --> 00:06:25,332
Five: make secrets dot E N V private, with mode six hundred.

202
00:06:25,882 --> 00:06:28,420
Then run lab check. Five pass lines.

203
00:06:30,470 --> 00:06:32,454
Six points, and you need all six.

204
00:06:33,004 --> 00:06:34,881
The checker shows five pass lines.

205
00:06:35,431 --> 00:06:40,061
You can explain authentication against authorization, with an example of each.

206
00:06:40,611 --> 00:06:43,192
You can explain four oh one against four oh three.

207
00:06:43,742 --> 00:06:47,113
You can send a bearer token, and say where a token comes from.

208
00:06:47,663 --> 00:06:52,548
You can say why secrets stay out of code and out of git, and how to lock a secrets file.

209
00:06:53,098 --> 00:06:55,829
You ran lab down, and nothing is left listening.

210
